; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Koch Curve, Step by Step
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, Koch curve, fractal, levels
; SUMMARY:  Draws the Koch curve at levels 0 to 4, one under the other, to show how it grows.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The top row is a plain line. On the next row its middle third
;   is replaced by a little tent. On every row after that, each
;   straight piece gets its own tent. Five rows show the rule
;   working, from simple to fancy.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try changing the colors or the row spacing.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the Koch rule: forward, left 60, right 120, left 60
;   * recursion where level 0 is just FORWARD
;   * FOR with a counter that is used as an input
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the tent point down by swapping LEFT and RIGHT.
;   * Turn 85 instead of 60 (and 170 instead of 120). What happens?
;   * Add a sixth row. Can you still see the difference?
; ============================================================

; KOCH draws one Koch curve of length :len.
to koch :len :level
  ; At level 0 there is nothing clever to do: just a straight line.
  if :level = 0 [forward :len stop]
  ; Otherwise the line is four lines a third as long, with a bump.
  koch :len / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  koch :len / 3 :level - 1
  right 120
  koch :len / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  koch :len / 3 :level - 1
end

; ROW draws one curve at the given level and height, with a caption.
to row :level :y
  penup setxy -330 :y + 5 pendown
  setpencolor 0
  label word "level| | :level
  penup setxy -180 :y setheading 90 pendown
  setpencolor item :level + 1 [1 10 13 4 14]
  ; A curve 360 long has a tent about 104 high, so rows 112 apart
  ; never bump into each other.
  koch 360 :level
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7
setpensize 2
for [level 0 4] [row :level 230 - :level * 112]
